	title = {Agiles {Lernen} zur {Kompetenzentwicklung} für {High} {Responsibility} {Teams}},
	copyright = {All rights reserved},
	url = {https://zenodo.org/records/15855879},
	abstract = {Agile learning has not yet been discussed in the context of competence development of high responsibility teams. These types of teams assume high responsibility for the lives of others or high material assets and place great value on error prevention. The suitability of the construct agile learning for competence development in high responsibility teams is answered by this actionable research question. The present theoretical conceptualization states that agile learning achieves good results and can be used as a didactic framework. Previous studies have investigated and described the impact mechanisms of agile sprint learning, and the results of this study form the basis of the present work. In order to answer the research question of competence development, the development of the specific definition of competence and the outline of the developmental process became necessary. Scrum can be used in the considered application area as an agile method to train high responsibility teams and develop their skills. The possibilities of agile learning become particularly clear in a precise, methodically structured implementation of these learning arrangements, which link cognitive and psycho-motor actions. Demonstrated and assessed in a state examination. Limits of agile learning are set by rigid rules and decoupled learning locations. The summary result of this conceptual work states that agile learning provides a context-situated framework that enables the development of competencies for teams with high levels of responsibility, resulting in positive outcomes.},
	language = {de-DE},
